WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.467
You're here. You made it.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.868
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.534
Well, let's get to some news.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.868
Well, guys, for everyone
invested in our country's banks,

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.667
March Madness has begun.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.534
Hey, a lot of people are talking
about this.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:19.767
Over the weekend, the U.S.
economy was rocked

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.167
after the Silicon Valley bank
crashed,

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:26.234
becoming the second largest bank
failure in U.S. history.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.801
It's never good when people who
are watching CNBC are shrieking

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.667
louder than the people watching
"Scream VI."

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:33.133
They're like, "Oh! Ah!"

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.534
Silicon Valley bank knew they
were in trouble when they saw

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.467
themselves in the Oscars
In Memoriam.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:40.634
They go, "Oh, that's us."

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.968
On the bright side, it was
refreshing to hear about a crash

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.033
that had nothing to do
with a self-driving Tesla.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.934
Don't you think?

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.334
In response to the crash, today,
President Biden delivered

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.067
a speech and ensured Americans
they can have confidence

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.801
that the banking system is safe.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.834
Hearing from Biden actually did
make me feel better

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.734
because you know if it were
really bad, he would've been

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.234
like, "Kamala,
you take this one."

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:03.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.501
"You did this one."

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:10.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.734
Biden tried to put everyone
at ease.

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.534
He said, "Don't worry.
I got through the first

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.400
Great Depression.
I'll get through this one."

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:22.167
Meanwhile, in response, Trump
said, "It's times like these

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.767
where we need a president
with experience

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.400
of multiple bankruptcies.
And that's --"

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.968
That's where I'm --"

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.834
Well, some sports news.
Everyone's excited about this.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:36.601
Yesterday was Selection Sunday,
where they announce the 68 teams

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:39.100
in this year's March Madness
tournament.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.434
Yep.

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.133
That's exciting.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.400
That's right.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.234
It starts at 68, then 32,
then eventually down to 1,

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.234
just like the number
of U.S. banks.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:52.200
And, yeah, first Oscar pools,
and now brackets --

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.334
it's that time of year when we
lose money to coworkers

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:55.701
we've never heard of before.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:59.567
It's like, "Who the hell is
Graham? I owe Graham $20."

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.300
Well, March Madness is about
to begin.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.734
There's so many great teams
this year.

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:06.467
Kansas, Purdue, Gonzaga --

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.300
is it Gonzaga or Gonzaga?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.734
I'm always forgetting how
they're pronounced.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.434
-Oh, come on. Come on.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:12.734
If you're going to talk about
the tournament, you've got to

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.901
know how to pronounce the names,
you know what I mean?

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.868
-Oh, so you know how to
pronounce all this year's

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.701
men's basketball teams?
-Not only that,

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:22.667
I know how to pronounce every
college basketball team.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.601
I'm an announcer.
Kind of my job.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:27.767
So, go ahead.
Test me, give me some names.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.567
-Give you some names --
all right, I guess I can

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.200
test you real quick.
Okay, what is this?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.434
What school is this?
-Oh, come on.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:33.801
Corn hole. Easy.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.567
-All right, how about this one?
How about this one?

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.467
-"Vanderpump Rules."
Come on, give me a hard one.

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:43.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.767
Rapid fire me.
-You want rapid fire?

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.200
All right, here we go.
Here we go. What's this?

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.934
-Okay. USB Cord.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:51.868
Charleton Heston.

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.701
Mary Jane.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.434
Burning Man.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.567
Liposuction.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:57.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:00.701
Oh, "Miss, I pee pee great."

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.567
Viagra.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.234
Prepubescence.

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.400
Stormy Daniel's book.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.300
Dookie.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.634
Oral sex robot.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:10.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.033
Sweet boning adventure.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.667
Oh, oh, this is Ken's ass.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.701
Oh, vagina.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:20.200
West vagina.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.234
Penis taint.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.300
Oh, I can't even believe you can
say this on TV.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.601
Ball state.

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:28.767
-Okay, that's enough.
Thank you.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:29.801
You're right. You're right.

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.100
You know how to pronounce them
all.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.634
Steve Higgins, everybody.
Steve Higgins.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.400
Sorry about that, yeah.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.601
Well, some big
entertainment news.

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.200
Last night was
the 95th Academy Awards.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.934
And I want to say congrats
to all the winners.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:45.300
"Everything Everywhere
All At Once" had a huge night,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.767
taking home seven awards.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:49.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.434
Meanwhile, the Oscars were on at
the same time

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.567
as the season finale
of "The Last of Us,"

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.567
and you could tell people
were a little distracted.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.033
Check this out.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:02.501
-It is my honor to be named
alongside you in this category.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:05.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:08.067
-You don't have to tell me all
of this.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.234
-Yeah, I actually do.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:10.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:14.200
-They had two --
They had two camera angles.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.434
-Yeah, two camera angles.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.567
There was a guy right over
his shoulder, yeah.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.467
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:21.367
Some more business news,
I heard that Apple is working

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.534
on AirPods that can improve
your hearing,

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:27.567
monitor your posture,
and take your temperature.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.868
Take your temperature?
People are like,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.434
